Consider a unity-gain negative feedback system consisting of the plant [latex]G(s)[/latex] (given below) and a proportional-integral controller. Let the proportional gain and integral gain be 3 and 1, respectively. For a unit step reference input, the final values of the controller output and the plant output, respectively, are [latex]
G(s)=\frac{1}{s-1}
[/latex]

The Fourier transform [latex]X(\omega)[/latex] of the signal [latex]x(t)[/latex] is given by [latex]
\begin{aligned}
X(\omega) & =1, \text { for }|\omega| \lt W_{0} \\
& =0, \text { for }|\omega| \gt W_{0}
\end{aligned}
[/latex] Which one of the following statements is true?

The discrete-time Fourier transform of a signal [latex]x[n][/latex] is [latex]X(\Omega)=1(1+\cos \Omega) e^{-j \Omega}[/latex]. Consider that [latex]x_{p}[n][/latex] is a periodic signal of period [latex]N=5[/latex] such that [latex]
\begin{aligned}
x_{p}[n] & =x[n], \text { for } n=0,1,2 \\
& =0, \text { for } n=3,4
\end{aligned}
[/latex] Note that [latex]x_{p}[n]=\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} a_{k} e^{j \frac{2 \pi}{N} k m}[/latex]. The magnitude of the Fourier series coefficient [latex]a_{3}[/latex] is ____ (Round off to 3 decimal places).
